<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Boyko Borisov</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1959">1959</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Boyko Borisov is a Bulgarian politician, a former chief secretary of the interior ministry and mayor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sofia">Sofia</a>, who founded the centre-right GERB party. He served as prime minister three times between 2009 and 2021 and dominated Bulgarian politics until mass anti-corruption protests in 2020 were followed by a series of snap elections.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/boyko-borisov.jpg" alt="Boyko Borisov" width="320" height="429" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: European People's Party · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:EPP_Congress_2025_Valencia_Day_1_(54484217152)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
